source: tests/rule_docs.rs
expression: render_rule_doc(rule.as_ref())
---
## `misnamed-suppression`

Report a suppression comment that names an unknown rule. Rule IDs must match exactly, so a misspelled ID suppresses nothing. When there is a single close match, the safe fix corrects the ID and keeps the reason.

A directive naming a rule that does not exist:

```julia
# fatou-ignore unused-bindings: set up by the C library
function f()
    handle = open_device()
    1
end
```

```text
warning: misnamed-suppression
 --> example.jl:1:16
  |
1 | # fatou-ignore unused-bindings: set up by the C library
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `unused-bindings` is not a fatou rule; this suppresses nothing
  = help: Replace with `unused-binding` (safe fix)
```

After applying the fix:

```julia
# fatou-ignore unused-binding: set up by the C library
function f()
    handle = open_device()
    1
end
```
